  "details": "Version: 944\nDescription: In any world, if your camera faces realtime lights when facing one of the cardinal directions (but I believe its specifically north) the realtime lights will turn off.\nSteps to reproduce (how did you encounter the bug?):\n1) Face north with a realtime light in your vision.\nAny extra files? (output logs, screenshots): \nVowgan made a map where I caught flickering (but this happens anywhere, ex. Japari Cafe (night) and Syntax Error Stockholm): https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/461679727049179177/721209420985663528/2020-06-12_23-46-29.mp4",
